"""Original systems and application security scenarios."""
ITEMS=[]
def group(o,rows):
 for k,(s,e) in enumerate(rows):ITEMS.append((s,[o[k]]+[v for j,v in enumerate(o) if j!=k],e))
group(['Application allowlisting','Endpoint behavior monitoring','Full-disk encryption','Host firewall enforcement'],[
('A workstation should execute only software permitted by an established application policy. Which endpoint control most directly enforces that execution boundary?', 'Application allowlisting restricts execution to the permitted policy set.'),
('A team needs visibility into suspicious process chains and associated endpoint activity to investigate possible compromise. Which capability directly supplies that telemetry?', 'Endpoint behavior monitoring provides activity evidence for detection and investigation.'),
('An organization wants to reduce disclosure from a stolen, powered-off laptop whose decryption key is unavailable to the thief. Which endpoint safeguard directly addresses this?', 'Full-disk encryption protects stored data under the stated key and device condition.'),
('A laptop must reject unsolicited inbound connections even when it is used outside the corporate perimeter. Which local control enforces that network rule?', 'A host firewall applies network policy at the endpoint, including away from the enterprise perimeter.')])
group(['Malicious software disguised as a useful tool','Self-propagating malicious software','Malicious software that encrypts for extortion','Software that covertly collects user information'],[
('An employee installs an apparent document utility that secretly performs unauthorized actions. Which malware behavior is illustrated?', 'A Trojan disguises malicious behavior within an apparently useful or legitimate program.'),
('A malicious program automatically spreads between vulnerable systems without needing a user to attach it to a separate host file. Which behavior is illustrated?', 'Worm-like behavior involves self-propagation between systems.'),
('A malicious program makes business files inaccessible and demands payment for recovery. Which behavior is illustrated?', 'Ransomware commonly uses encryption or other denial of access for extortion; payment does not guarantee recovery.'),
('An unauthorized program silently records browsing and user activity for an outside party. Which behavior is illustrated?', 'Spyware covertly collects information about users or their activity.')])
group(['Verify through a known independent channel','Report the suspicious message','Revoke the exposed credential','Preserve the relevant message evidence'],[
('A convincing email requests an urgent change to a supplier’s payment account. Before authorizing any change, what action directly validates the request?', 'Use a previously established independent contact method rather than contact details supplied in the unverified request.'),
('An employee receives a suspected phishing message, has not interacted with it and is instructed to use the organization’s reporting mechanism. What should the employee do?', 'Report through the designated channel so the security team can assess and respond.'),
('A user entered an account password into a confirmed fraudulent page. The account owner is coordinating with responders. Which credential action addresses continued misuse?', 'Revoke or replace the exposed credential and address active sessions through the response process.'),
('Responders are investigating a targeted impersonation attempt and need its original headers and content. Which handling action supports their analysis?', 'Preserve relevant message evidence using the approved process rather than altering or discarding the original.')])
group(['Mobile device management','Mobile application management','Separation of work and personal data','An approved remote wipe process'],[
('An organization needs to enforce managed phone configuration, inventory and compliance requirements across enrolled devices. Which capability fits?', 'Mobile device management governs device-level configuration and compliance.'),
('A company needs controls focused on its business applications and their data on permitted mobile devices. Which capability fits?', 'Mobile application management applies policy at the application and business-data level.'),
('A bring-your-own-device program must keep organizational documents distinct from the owner’s personal photos and messages. Which design principle addresses this boundary?', 'Separate work and personal data through an appropriate managed boundary and clear policy.'),
('A managed phone containing sensitive work data is lost. Policy and authorization specify removing protected data remotely when the device reconnects. Which response capability is needed?', 'An authorized remote wipe process can remove the designated data when technically reachable; it is not a guarantee that an offline device was wiped.')])
group(['Infrastructure as a Service','Platform as a Service','Software as a Service','Customer-managed on-premises hosting'],[
('A provider supplies virtual machines and storage while the customer manages the guest operating system and applications. Which service model is this?', 'IaaS supplies infrastructure while leaving guest operating systems and applications under customer management.'),
('A provider manages the operating system and runtime, while the customer deploys its own application into that supported environment. Which service model is this?', 'PaaS provides a managed application platform while the customer controls its deployed application.'),
('Employees use a provider-operated business application through a browser and configure permitted user settings. Which service model is this?', 'SaaS provides the application itself, with limited customer configuration rather than management of the underlying stack.'),
('An organization owns and operates the physical servers, operating systems and application in its own facility. No external cloud service is involved. Which hosting arrangement is described?', 'This is customer-managed on-premises hosting, with the stated stack operated by the organization.')])
group(['A private cloud deployment','A public cloud deployment','A community cloud deployment','A hybrid cloud deployment'],[
('A cloud environment is provisioned for the exclusive use of one organization with multiple business units. Which deployment model fits?', 'A private cloud is for exclusive organizational use and can be operated on or off premises.'),
('A provider offers cloud services for open use by the general public. Which deployment model fits?', 'A public cloud is provisioned for open use by the general public, subject to service agreements.'),
('Several organizations with shared compliance concerns use a cloud provisioned exclusively for that defined community. Which deployment model fits?', 'A community cloud serves a defined group with shared concerns.'),
('Distinct private and public cloud environments remain separate but are connected by technology enabling data and application portability. Which deployment model fits?', 'A hybrid cloud combines distinct cloud infrastructures with the stated binding capability.')])
group(['Patch the guest operating system','Review tenant access permissions','Assess the provider’s assurance evidence','Define service exit requirements'],[
('An IaaS contract assigns guest operating-system maintenance to the customer. A guest security update is due. Which responsibility must the customer perform?', 'The customer must patch the guest under the stated responsibility model; provider infrastructure maintenance does not replace this duty.'),
('A SaaS provider protects its infrastructure, but the customer has made a confidential workspace accessible to every employee. Which customer action addresses the identified issue?', 'Review and correct tenant permissions. Provider infrastructure protection does not determine the customer’s appropriate sharing policy.'),
('Before approving a cloud supplier, an organization needs evidence about the supplier’s relevant controls and the scope of independent assessments. Which activity fits?', 'Assess applicable assurance evidence and its scope rather than infer control effectiveness from a marketing claim.'),
('A business may leave its current cloud service next year and must preserve access to its records in a usable form. Which contractual planning task addresses this?', 'Define exit, data export, retention and disposal requirements before dependence makes migration difficult.')])
group(['A type 1 hypervisor','A type 2 hypervisor','Operating-system-level containers','A virtual machine snapshot'],[
('Virtual machines run under a hypervisor installed directly on the hardware without a general-purpose host operating system beneath it. Which architecture is this?', 'A type 1 hypervisor runs directly on the hardware.'),
('A desktop virtualization application runs on top of an existing general-purpose host operating system. Which architecture is this?', 'A type 2 hypervisor is hosted by an operating system.'),
('Several isolated application environments share the host kernel rather than each running a separate guest kernel. Which architecture is this?', 'Operating-system-level containers share the host kernel, making host isolation and hardening important.'),
('An administrator records a virtual machine’s state at a particular point for a controlled short-term rollback. Which artifact is created?', 'A snapshot records a point-in-time state. It should not automatically be treated as an independent protected backup.')])
group(['Harden the virtualization management plane','Limit unnecessary host integration','Control image provenance','Remove abandoned virtual machines'],[
('One administrative console can change every virtual machine in a cluster. Which security focus addresses the concentrated privilege of that console?', 'Protect the management plane with restricted access, strong authentication, monitoring and approved changes.'),
('A sensitive guest has unneeded shared folders and device passthrough links to its host. Which hardening change reduces those extra interaction paths?', 'Remove unnecessary host integration to reduce exposure while preserving required functionality.'),
('A team wants to deploy a virtual appliance downloaded from an unverified mirror. Which supply-chain check is needed before trusting it?', 'Validate provenance and integrity through the authorized source and approval process.'),
('A cluster contains unused test guests with old credentials and no owner. Which lifecycle action reduces this unmanaged exposure?', 'Identify ownership and retire abandoned guests through the approved process, including retained data handling.')])
group(['Parameterize database values','Encode output for its context','Authorize each object request','Validate software dependencies'],[
('An application builds database commands by mixing user-supplied values into executable query text. Which development change separates values from query structure?', 'Parameterized queries keep supplied values distinct from the command structure when used correctly.'),
('A web page displays untrusted text within HTML. Which protection ensures the text is treated as data in that output context?', 'Use appropriate contextual output encoding or safe text rendering so untrusted content is not interpreted as executable markup.'),
('A signed-in user changes a record identifier and receives another customer’s private record. Which server-side check is missing?', 'The service must authorize access to the requested object for the current user, not merely verify that someone is signed in.'),
('An application imports an outdated library with a known security flaw. Which lifecycle activity directly addresses this component exposure?', 'Track and evaluate dependencies, then update or otherwise mitigate the affected component under a controlled process.')])
assert len(ITEMS)==40
